@page
@model BeeMemoryBank.Web.Pages.Admin.RestoredDevicesModel

@section About {
    <p>
        When you restore a snapshot, this node gets back the list of devices it trusted at that moment. For each device it asks for proof: an integrity anchor,
        signed under your master key, that names the device and its key. A device with that proof comes back switched on. A device without it comes back
        <strong>switched off</strong>: it cannot sign in with its key, sync or write anything here until you decide about it.
    </p>
    <p>
        This page lists those devices. <strong>Confirm the ones you recognise</strong> (they are yours, and you know their names and addresses): they sync with
        this node again. A confirmed device does not get superadmin rights back by itself; if it should have them, promote it on
        <a href="/Admin/TrustedNodes">Trusted Nodes</a>. For a device you do not recognise, do nothing here: it stays off, and it can join again by
        being paired from scratch.
    </p>
    <p>The list is empty unless a restore left devices waiting.</p>
}

@if (Model.RestoredPeers.Count == 0)
{
    <div class="card" id="restored-devices-empty" style="text-align:center;padding:40px;">
        <sl-icon name="shield-check" style="font-size:2rem;color:var(--text-secondary);display:block;margin-bottom:12px;"></sl-icon>
        <p class="text-muted" style="margin:0;">No device is waiting for your confirmation.</p>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <div class="card" id="restored-peers">
        @foreach (var peer in Model.RestoredPeers)
        {
            <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
                <span style="flex:1;min-width:200px;"><strong>@peer.DisplayName</strong> <code style="font-size:0.78rem;">@peer.NodeId</code> @peer.ApiAddress</span>
                <form data-busy="short" method="post" asp-page-handler="ConfirmRestoredPeer" style="display:inline;">
                    <input type="hidden" name="nodeId" value="@peer.NodeId" />
                    <sl-button size="small" type="submit">Confirm</sl-button>
                </form>
            </div>
        }
    </div>
}
